From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:26:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j713: Add the CPU thermal zone

PMP's fast die loop catches load steps, but under sustained all-core
load the hot spot still creeps past its limit by about 0.1 C a second.
Add a power_allocator zone on TCMz, the hottest of the CPU sensors, and
aim it at 105 C: replayed on this machine, the clocks macOS picks keep
the hot spot between 100 and 107 C.

Only the P cores push the hot spot that far. At full clock the E
cluster draws about 3.6 W and stays below 80 C, so leave it out.

With integral_cutoff at 0 the integral only ever winds down, so add a
switch-on trip at 65 C. Below it power_allocator resets, which drops
the throttle an earlier load left behind once the CPUs have gone idle.
A sustainable power of 17 W lets a new load start at full clock and
leaves the first seconds to PMP's loop.

A step load on the P cluster overshoots PMP's 110 C to about 114 C
before the cap settles, so the critical trip sits at 118 C.

The gains power_allocator estimates for this range limit-cycle between
95 and 115 C, so tuned gains are expected from userspace.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts | 49 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
index 472a05969bcb..1067dc1ab9db 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713.dts
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include "t8132.dtsi"
 #include "t8132-jxxx.dtsi"
 #include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/thermal/thermal.h>
 
 / {
 	compatible = "apple,j713", "apple,t8132", "apple,arm-platform";
@@ -35,6 +36,52 @@ led-0 {
 			max-brightness = <255>;
 		};
 	};
+
+	thermal-zones {
+		/*
+		 * PMP's fast die loop catches load steps, but under sustained
+		 * all-core load the hot spot keeps creeping up past it by about
+		 * 0.1 C a second. Hold it at 105 C, where macOS holds it, and
+		 * reset the controller once the CPUs have gone idle.
+		 */
+		cpu-thermal {
+			polling-delay-passive = <500>;
+			polling-delay = <500>;
+			thermal-sensors = <&smc_hwmon 4>;
+			sustainable-power = <17000>;
+
+			trips {
+				cpu-switch-on {
+					temperature = <65000>;
+					hysteresis = <0>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
+				cpu_control: cpu-control {
+					temperature = <105000>;
+					hysteresis = <0>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
+				cpu-critical {
+					temperature = <118000>;
+					hysteresis = <0>;
+					type = "critical";
+				};
+			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&cpu_control>;
+					cooling-device =
+						<&cpu_p0 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+						<&cpu_p1 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+						<&cpu_p2 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>,
+						<&cpu_p3 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &wifi0 {
@@ -281,6 +328,8 @@ &ps_nub_spi0 {
 #include "hwmon-laptop.dtsi"
 
 &smc_hwmon {
+	#thermal-sensor-cells = <1>;
+
 	current-IP0b {
 		label = "P-cluster Rail Current";
 		apple,key-id = "IP0b";
